# BuildKit per-Dockerfile ignore file for deploy/images/kernel/Dockerfile.
#
# The kernel image's build context is the repository ROOT, whose working
# checkout carries ~839 MB of node_modules. Without this file every build would
# upload all of it.
#
# It lives here rather than at the repo root because the root `.gitignore`
# ignores `.dockerignore` (a pre-existing "Preview Docker test setup" rule), so
# a root ignore-file could not be committed alongside the deployment it belongs
# to. BuildKit resolves `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` relative to the context
# and prefers it over the context root's `.dockerignore`.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Local runtime state is never shipped in.
midnight-level-db*
packages/batcher/batcher-data

.git
.github
docs/dist
docs/node_modules
*-debug.log
.DS_Store

# The deployment's own generated state must never enter an image layer.
deploy/.env
deploy/**/.env

# Test code is not part of the runtime. Every file that only tests use carries
# `.test` in its name (`*.test.ts`, `*.test-<role>.ts`, `*.testkit.ts`,
# `*.pgtest.ts`), and benchmarks end in `*.bench.ts`; none of them, no test
# fixture and no part of the e2e suite enters the image. The e2e suite's
# manifest stays: the Dockerfile copies every workspace manifest before
# `bun install --frozen-lockfile`. deploy/images/kernel/image.test-gate.ts
# checks the built image against this list.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test-*.ts
**/*.testkit.ts
**/*.pgtest.ts
**/*.bench.ts
packages/tests
!packages/tests/package.json
packages/api-contracts/fixtures
packages/database/fixtures
packages/validator/fixtures
